<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australian Sept qtr house prices rise 0.4 pct.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australian Sept qtr house prices rise 0.4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian house prices rose 0.4 percent in the September quarter from the previous quarter and were 1.2 percent higher than a year earlier, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>The biggest quarterly rise was 0.9 percent in Darwin, for a rise of 4.1 percent for the year to September 30, the bureau said.</p>
<p>Hobart saw the biggest fall for the quarter of 0.8 percent.</p>
<p>The data covers established houses and detached residential dwellings on their own blocks of land. It includes new houses sold as house and land packages.</p>
<p>Here is a list of the percentage changes in the index for the eight capital cities covered:  </p>
<p>    City	     Sept quarter	  Annual</p>
<p>    Sydney	   0.7		     1.5</p>
<p>    Melbourne	0.3		     2.6</p>
<p>    Brisbane	 0.3		     0.4</p>
<p>    Perth	   -0.2		    -0.6</p>
<p>    Adelaide	-0.1		    -2.0</p>
<p>    Hobart	  -0.8		     0.8</p>
<p>    Canberra	-0.2		    -0.6</p>
<p>    Darwin	   0.9		     4.1</p>
<p>-- Canberra Bureau 61-6 273-2730</p>
</text>
